      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ZIPPING CHOI (1) hit the ground running from the squeeze draw with a slick early split, holding on for a minor placing when third and beaten 1.75 lengths at Geelong over 400m in 22.87. Remains without a win from the draw but has been in the placings two times from four attempts. Well-placed to take this out. ZIPPING NUTTALL (4) missed the frame last time out when sixth at this track from Box eight (24.72) but draws same box here as latest win. Boasts a strong record from this draw with two wins and two minor placings from four starts. Cannot be taken lightly. DR. WARREN (6) put in a much better performance last start when in the placings at this track behind Why Not Seb (24.21) in a Grade 5. Has the pace to be prominent. Goes well out of this box with a win and two minor placings. Expected to feature. PRINCESS DOMI (2) will give backers a sight.",
